   "design": "The dive computer's recorded profile is downloaded into a digital dive log, which fills times and depths, instead of the diver copying them by hand; the diver adds the task notes and the supervisor signs. Equipment checks, decompression planning, the briefing, registering the dive, monitoring and near-miss reports stay with the diver.",
   "previous_blocker": "Dive times and depths were copied from the dive computer by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Dive computers whose profiles download to a log.",
   "still_hard": "Dives where the computer fails and the log is rebuilt from the panel.",
   "human_edge": "Calling off a dive when conditions feel wrong.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less log copying; safety judgement stays.",
